  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.13,
      255.69,
      523.67,
      275.2
    ],
    "text": "Appeal quoted with approval the dictum of Whitemeyer J. in Rex V. Blom",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.548726081848145,
      13.450468063354492,
      13.734054565429688,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.272614479064941,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.47,
      276.8,
      123.73,
      296.32
    ],
    "text": "as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.328614234924316,
      14.199999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      50.79,
      306.1,
      523.06,
      346.48
    ],
    "text": "Two cardinal rules of logic governs the use of circumstantial evidence in the criminal trial:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.053948402404785,
      14.100752830505371,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.611827850341797,
      14.746484756469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.82,
      356.24,
      524.59,
      375.76
    ],
    "text": "(l)The inference sought to be drawn must be consistent with all the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.103421211242676,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.334512710571289,
      14.4979248046875
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.45,
      377.62,
      488.47,
      397.13
    ],
    "text": "approved facts. If it does not, then the inference cannot be drawn.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.199999809265137,
      14.525959014892578,
      14.641098976135254
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.83,
      406.9,
      523.78,
      426.41
    ],
    "text": "(2)The proof of facts should be such that they exclude every reasonable",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.103421211242676,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.262164115905762,
      14.331738471984863,
      14.338672637939453
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.82,
      428.24,
      524.03,
      447.76
    ],
    "text": "inference from them, save the one to be drawn. If they had not excluded",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.046772956848145,
      14.103421211242676,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.222282409667969,
      14.307293891906738,
      14.4979248046875,
      14.525959014892578
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.29,
      449.62,
      525.23,
      490.25
    ],
    "text": "the other reasonable inferences, then there must be a doubt whether the inferences sought to be drawn is correct.\"",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.580537796020508,
      14.103421211242676,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.230766296386719,
      14.248268127441406,
      14.4979248046875
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.51,
      500.0,
      524.45,
      540.41
    ],
    "text": "There is no direct evidence as to the identity of the accused in this case. The item of evidence relied by the prosecution is purely circumstantial.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.328614234924316,
      13.580537796020508,
      14.027299880981445,
      14.129173278808594,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.611827850341797,
      14.631542205810547,
      14.746484756469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      51.53,
      542.01,
      524.9,
      582.65
    ],
    "text": "On a perusal of the judgment of the learned trial Judge it is very clear that the trial judge had not considered all the material evidence that had",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.580537796020508,
      13.802331924438477,
      14.188495635986328,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.224827766418457,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.265847206115723,
      14.39732837677002,
      14.611827850341797,
      14.641098976135254,
      14.746484756469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      52.29,
      584.24,
      364.73,
      603.76
    ],
    "text": "been led before him at the trial by both parties.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.199999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      52.1,
      613.53,
      525.5,
      675.04
    ],
    "text": "Consideration of circumstantial evidence has been vividly described by Pollock C.B in Regina V.Exall [1866] 4 F&F 922 at page, cited in King V. Guneratne [1946] 47 N.L.R 145 at page 149 in the following words:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.309636116027832,
      13.431451797485352,
      13.839422225952148,
      13.915143013000488,
      14.052534103393555,
      14.149309158325195,
      14.181938171386719,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.219985961914062,
      14.292994499206543,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.9,
      69.94,
      527.21,
      89.45
    ],
    "text": "lilt has been said that circumstantial evidence is to be considered as a",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica",
      "Helvetica-Oblique"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.966031074523926,
      13.186803817749023,
      13.456114768981934,
      13.971511840820312,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.265847206115723,
      14.4979248046875
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.39,
      91.28,
      528.08,
      195.28
    ],
    "text": "chain, and each piece as a link in the chain, but that is not so, for then, if anyone link breaks, the chain would fall. It is more like the case of a rope comprised of several chords. One strand of the rope might be insufficient to sustain the weight; but three strands together may be quire of sufficient strength. Thus it may be in circumstantial evidence - there may",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.328614234924316,
      13.38511848449707,
      13.580537796020508,
      13.964496612548828,
      14.05410099029541,
      14.103421211242676,
      14.161347389221191,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.307293891906738,
      14.35416316986084,
      14.36306381225586,
      14.39732837677002,
      14.475919723510742,
      14.611827850341797,
      14.641098976135254,
      14.746484756469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.84,
      197.13,
      527.35,
      237.77
    ],
    "text": "be a combination of circumstances, no one of which raise a reasonable conviction or more than a mere suspicion; but the three taken together",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.103421211242676,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.475919723510742,
      14.746484756469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      54.18,
      239.61,
      526.54,
      259.13
    ],
    "text": "may create a conclusion of guilt with as much certainty as human affairs",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.456114768981934,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.334512710571289,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.6,
      260.73,
      201.15,
      280.25
    ],
    "text": "can require or admit.\"",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.933091163635254,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.289617538452148
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.43,
      290.26,
      527.5,
      352.0
    ],
    "text": "The items of circumstantial evidence referred to earlier in this case in my opinion is insufficient to sustain the weight of the rope. Further totality of the evidence led in this case does not lead to an inescapable",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.38511848449707,
      13.964496612548828,
      14.047126770019531,
      14.129173278808594,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.224827766418457,
      14.271121978759766,
      14.4979248046875,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.54,
      361.76,
      526.07,
      402.41
    ],
    "text": "And irresistible inference and conclusion that it was the accused-appellant who inflicted injuries on the deceased. The prosecution has",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.890067100524902,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.308287620544434,
      14.331738471984863,
      14.410538673400879
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      53.97,
      404.24,
      527.35,
      423.76
    ],
    "text": "failed to prove the case beyond reasonable doubt and rebut the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      13.964496612548828,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.203399658203125,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.4979248046875
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      54.45,
      425.61,
      231.83,
      445.13
    ],
    "text": "presumption of innocence.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.199999809265137,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      54.62,
      454.64,
      527.24,
      474.16
    ],
    "text": "For the reasons enumerated by me, on the facts and the law, in the",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.17582893371582,
      14.199999809265137,
      14.227672576904297,
      14.308287620544434
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      54.07,
      476.01,
      527.04,
      537.76
    ],
    "text": "foregoing paragraphs of this judgment, I set aside the conviction and sentence of the Learned High Court Judge of Monaragala dated 02.09.2014 and acquit the accused-appellant.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.199999809265137,
      14.308287620544434,
      14.611827850341797
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
      54.01,
      547.53,
      161.68,
      567.04
    ],
    "text": "Appeal allowed.",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.199999809265137
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 6,
    "bbox": [
